	abstract = {This special issue of Discourse Processes highlights work presented at the 35th annual meeting of The Society for Text & Discourse (ST&D) held in Padua, Italy in July 2025. The special issue opens with the thought-provoking contribution by Arthur Glenberg, the winner of the ST&D Distinguished Scientific Contribution Award in 2025. The conference-based special collection then includes contributions regarding a range of relevant issues and challenges of research in four main areas: (1) reading, evaluating, and comprehending digital texts; (2) reading processes and outcomes; (3) spatial representations as tools for effective discourse processing and comprehension; and (4) discourse-based complex problem-solving. The contributions highlight that attention should be paid to the real context where cognitive processes are activated, the importance of motivational-emotional drivers while understanding written and oral discourse, and the use of up-to-date statistical procedures. The multidisciplinary and international character of our society is also well reflected in the contributions. © 2026 Taylor & Francis Group, LLC.},
